return [
    'Getting Started' => [

        'System overview' => [
            'body' => '<p>The MAIIC IFRS 9 platform is the single system in which the corporation measures Expected Credit Loss (ECL, the provision IFRS 9 requires against every loan) and Effective Interest Rate revenue (EIR, the rate that spreads fees and interest evenly over the life of a loan). Every figure on every screen is read from the database for the reporting period you have selected. Nothing is typed in by hand or fixed in the software. The platform is used by credit risk analysts who load data and run the models, by finance staff who review the results and sign off the month, and by administrators who look after users, periods and settings.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><p>The dark green sidebar on the left lists every part of the platform in the order in which work normally flows. The groups, top to bottom, are:</p><ul><li><b>Dashboard</b>: the one-page position for a period.</li><li><b>Workspace</b>: the ten-step month-end close checklist and team messages.</li><li><b>Reports</b>: IFRS 9 Reports (the full report catalogue), ECL Reconciliation, Loan Book Reconciliation, Disbursements (Vintage) and Stress Testing.</li><li><b>Portfolio Setup</b>: Loan Portfolios, Sector Types and Product Groups, the reference lists that segment the loan book.</li><li><b>Customer &amp; Loan Data</b>: Clients, Loan Book and Imports, where the month-end extract is loaded and checked.</li><li><b>Collateral Management</b>: Collateral Register, Collateral Types and Collateral Allocation.</li><li><b>EIR &amp; Revenue Recognition</b>: Accounting Rules, EIR Data, Fee Classification, EIR Calculations, GL Reconciliation and Coverage &amp; Blockers.</li><li><b>IFRS 9 Model Setup</b>: five sub-groups. Staging &amp; SICR Rules (Quantitative Thresholds, SICR Groups Setup, SICR Alert Items, SICR Trigger Alerts), PD Model Setup (Transition Profiles, Monthly Probability, Cumulative Probability, Internal Grades), LGD Model Setup (Monthly LGD, Cumulative LGD), Forward-Looking Model (Macro Elements, Scenario Profiles, Weighted Forecast, Credit Loss Data, Adjusted Forecast, Regression Analysis) and Management Overlays (Economic Scenarios, External Calculations, Calculation History).</li><li><b>ECL Processing</b>: ECL Calculation, the engine run itself.</li><li><b>System Documentation</b>: User Manual, Administrator Manual, Technical Manual and Installation Guide.</li><li><b>Administration</b>: User Management, Roles &amp; Permissions, Financial Periods, Audit Trail, Support Tickets and Settings.</li></ul><h4>The reporting period</h4><p>Almost every screen is scoped to a <b>reporting period</b>, a calendar month written as year and month, for example <code>2025-11</code>. The loan book is imported once per period, the models are applied to that period, ECL is calculated for it, and the reports and the Dashboard read it back. When you change the period in a green period pill or a filter bar, every table, tile and chart on that page is re-read from the database for the new period. The Dashboard only offers periods for which ECL has already been calculated; the Workspace offers every period that has a loan book.</p><h4>Roles</h4><p>Access is controlled by roles. The system ships with one built-in role, <b>Administrator</b>, which holds every permission: administrators can import data, run models, tick the manual steps of the Workspace checklist, edit the manuals, manage users and change settings. Further roles are created on the Roles &amp; Permissions screen by choosing exactly which permissions a role should have; a user with a restricted role sees the same sidebar, but any page or button outside their permissions is hidden or refused with a <b>No access rights</b> message. If you cannot see a menu item you expect, ask an administrator to review your role.</p><h4>How the work flows</h4><ol><li>Set up portfolios, sector types and product groups.</li><li>Import the loan book for the period and check the Loan Book screen.</li><li>Allocate collateral and load EIR schedules and fees.</li><li>Apply staging rules, the PD model, the LGD model and the forward-looking adjustment.</li><li>Run the ECL Calculation.</li><li>Review the reports, run stress scenarios and sign the period off in the Workspace.</li></ol><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>A page shows no data.</b> Check the reporting period selector first; most screens open on the latest period that has data.</li><li><b>A menu item is missing.</b> Your role does not include that permission.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Sign in with your email address, password and the security code.',
                'Read the Dashboard for the latest calculated period to see the current position.',
                'Open Workspace to see which of the ten close steps are still outstanding for the period you are working on.',
                'Work down the sidebar in order: Portfolio Setup, Customer & Loan Data, Collateral Management, EIR & Revenue Recognition, IFRS 9 Model Setup, ECL Processing.',
                'Read the results under Reports and raise anything that needs attention as a Support Ticket under Administration.',
            ],
            'images' => ['dashboard' => 'The sidebar lists the module groups in the order in which work flows; the Dashboard is the landing page after sign-in'],
        ],

        'Signing in and the security check' => [
            'body' => '<p>The sign-in page is the first screen you see when you open the platform address in your browser. Anyone with an account uses it; accounts are created by an administrator under Administration, User Management, and the first password is sent to you by email. Sign-in is protected by a security check (a CAPTCHA, an image of characters that a person can read but an automated program cannot) which is generated on the MAIIC server itself, so nothing about your visit is sent to any outside service.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li><b>Left panel</b> (wide screens only): the MAIIC logo, the strapline <b>Investing in Potential. Building Futures.</b>, the green, gold and red brand bar and the corporation\'s sector icons. It is decorative.</li><li><b>Sign-in card</b> with a green hexagon user badge, the heading <b>Welcome back</b> and the line <b>Sign in to access your account</b>.</li><li><b>Email address</b>: a box with an envelope icon and the prompt <b>Enter your email</b>.</li><li><b>Password</b>: a box with a padlock icon and the prompt <b>Enter your password</b>. The crossed-eye button at the right end (titled <b>Show password</b>, then <b>Hide password</b>) reveals or hides what you have typed.</li><li><b>Remember me</b>: a tick box that keeps you signed in on this browser after you close it.</li><li><b>Forgot password?</b>: a green link to the password reset page.</li><li><b>Security check</b>: an image showing five large green, slate and gold characters on a speckled background, a grey button with a circular-arrows icon titled <b>Get a new code</b>, and a box with the prompt <b>Enter the code shown above</b>. Under it the note <b>Type the characters shown above. Not case-sensitive.</b></li><li><b>Sign in</b>: the full-width green button with an arrow. While the server is checking it reads <b>Signing in…</b> and cannot be pressed twice.</li><li>A shield icon and the footer <b>Secure. Reliable. Committed to Growth.</b></li></ul><h4>Field by field</h4><ul><li><b>Email address</b>: the address your administrator registered, for example <code>analyst@maiic.mw</code>. Required.</li><li><b>Password</b>: your current password. Required. It is cleared after every attempt.</li><li><b>Security check</b>: the five characters in the image, typed in any case. The image never contains the digits 0 or 1 or the letters O, I or L, so there is no ambiguity. Each code is valid for five minutes and for one attempt only; a fresh image is drawn after every attempt and whenever you press <b>Get a new code</b>.</li></ul><h4>To reset a forgotten password</h4><ol><li>Press <b>Forgot password?</b> on the sign-in page.</li><li>Read the note: <b>Forgot your password? No problem. Just let us know your email address and we will email you a password reset link that will allow you to choose a new one.</b></li><li>Type your address in <b>Email</b> and press <b>Email Password Reset Link</b>.</li><li>Open the link in the email. On the reset page complete <b>Email</b>, <b>Password</b> and <b>Confirm Password</b> and press <b>Reset Password</b>.</li></ol><h4>If two-factor authentication is switched on</h4><p>After the password is accepted you are taken to a second page that says <b>Please confirm access to your account by entering the authentication code provided by your authenticator application.</b> Type the six-digit number from your phone in <b>Code</b> and press <b>Log in</b>. If your phone is not to hand, press <b>Use a recovery code</b>, type one of your saved recovery codes in <b>Recovery Code</b> and press <b>Log in</b>; <b>Use an authentication code</b> switches back. Each recovery code works once.</p><h4>What happens next</h4><p>On success you land on the IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard. Your sign-in is recorded against your account and appears under Browser Sessions on your Profile page.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The security code is incorrect or has expired. Please enter the new code shown.</b> The characters did not match, or more than five minutes passed. A new image has already been drawn; type the new code and try again.</li><li><b>These credentials do not match our records.</b> The email or password is wrong. Check for a stale saved password in your browser, then use <b>Forgot password?</b> if needed.</li><li><b>Too many attempts.</b> After five failed attempts from the same address within one minute the server refuses further attempts for a short while (error code 429). Wait a minute and try again.</li><li><b>The code image is blank.</b> Press <b>Get a new code</b>. If it stays blank, tell your administrator: the image library on the server may be missing.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Open the platform address in your browser.',
                'Type your registered address in Email address.',
                'Type your password in Password. Press the eye button if you want to check what you typed.',
                'Tick Remember me if this is your own computer and you want to stay signed in.',
                'Read the five characters in the Security check image and type them in the box below it. Press the circular-arrows button (Get a new code) if the image is hard to read.',
                'Press Sign in. If two-factor authentication is on, enter the code from your phone and press Log in.',
                'You land on the IFRS 9 ECL Dashboard.',
            ],
            'images' => ['login' => 'The sign-in page: email, password with show and hide button, Remember me, Forgot password?, the security check image with its refresh button, and the Sign in button'],
            'routes' => ['login', 'password.request', 'password.reset', 'two-factor.login'],
        ],

        'Your profile, password and two-factor authentication' => [
            'body' => '<p>The Profile page is where you look after your own account: your name, email address and photo, your password, two-factor authentication, the browsers you are signed in on, and account deletion. Every signed-in user has one. To reach it, press the round avatar at the far right of the top header and choose <b>Profile</b> from the menu.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li>Page title <b>Profile</b>. There is no help button on this page.</li><li><b>Profile Information</b>: the panel on the right has <b>Photo</b> (your current picture, or a coloured circle with your initial), the button <b>SELECT A NEW PHOTO</b>, <b>Remove Photo</b> (only once a photo has been uploaded), the fields <b>Name</b> and <b>Email</b>, and a green <b>SAVE</b> button. A small <b>Saved.</b> message appears beside the button after a successful save.</li><li><b>Update Password</b>: <b>Current Password</b>, <b>New Password</b>, <b>Confirm Password</b> and <b>SAVE</b>, again with <b>Saved.</b> on success.</li><li><b>Two Factor Authentication</b>: a heading reading either <b>You have not enabled two factor authentication.</b> or <b>You have enabled two factor authentication.</b>, an explanation, and the buttons <b>Enable</b> (when off) or <b>Regenerate Recovery Codes</b>, <b>Show Recovery Codes</b> and the red <b>Disable</b> (when on). After enabling, a QR code and a grey box of recovery codes are shown.</li><li><b>Browser Sessions</b>: a list of recent sign-ins, each showing platform and browser, the network address, and either <b>This device</b> in green or <b>Last active</b> followed by a time. Below it the button <b>Log Out Other Browser Sessions</b> and the message <b>Done.</b> after success.</li><li><b>Delete Account</b>: a warning and a red <b>Delete Account</b> button.</li></ul><h4>Field by field</h4><ul><li><b>Photo</b>: any image file; it is shown as a circle in the header. Optional.</li><li><b>Name</b>: your display name as it appears on tickets, workspace messages and the audit trail. Required.</li><li><b>Email</b>: your sign-in address. Required and must be unique.</li><li><b>Current Password</b>: required; the new password is refused if it is wrong.</li><li><b>New Password</b> and <b>Confirm Password</b>: at least eight characters and both boxes must match.</li></ul><h4>To change your password</h4><ol><li>Under <b>Update Password</b>, type your existing password in <b>Current Password</b>.</li><li>Type the new password in <b>New Password</b> and again in <b>Confirm Password</b>.</li><li>Press <b>SAVE</b> and wait for <b>Saved.</b></li></ol><h4>To switch on two-factor authentication</h4><ol><li>Install an authenticator app on your phone (for example Google Authenticator).</li><li>Under <b>Two Factor Authentication</b> press <b>Enable</b>.</li><li>A <b>Confirm Password</b> box appears with the text <b>For your security, please confirm your password to continue.</b> Type your password and press <b>Confirm</b> (or <b>Nevermind</b> to stop).</li><li>Scan the QR code with the app. The heading changes to <b>Two factor authentication is now enabled. Scan the following QR code using your phone\'s authenticator application.</b></li><li>Copy the recovery codes from the grey box into a password manager or another safe place; the page says <b>Store these recovery codes in a secure password manager.</b></li></ol><p>From now on every sign-in asks for the six-digit code after your password. <b>Regenerate Recovery Codes</b> replaces the codes with a new set (the old ones stop working); <b>Show Recovery Codes</b> displays the current set; <b>Disable</b> switches the feature off. Each of these asks for your password first.</p><h4>To sign out of other devices</h4><ol><li>Under <b>Browser Sessions</b> press <b>Log Out Other Browser Sessions</b>.</li><li>Type your password in the box and press <b>Log Out Other Browser Sessions</b> in the dialogue, or <b>Nevermind</b> to cancel.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>A new name is used immediately across the platform. A changed password takes effect on your next sign-in. Deleting your account (<b>Delete Account</b>, then your password, then <b>Delete Account</b> in the dialogue) removes your user permanently; records you created, such as tickets and messages, keep your name as text.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The provided password does not match your current password.</b> Retype <b>Current Password</b>.</li><li><b>The password confirmation does not match.</b> The two new-password boxes differ.</li><li><b>The email has already been taken.</b> Another user already uses that address.</li><li><b>I lost my phone.</b> Sign in with a recovery code, then press <b>Disable</b> and <b>Enable</b> again to pair a new phone. If you have no codes left, an administrator must reset your account.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Press the round avatar at the top right of any page and choose Profile.',
                'Under Profile Information, change Name or Email, or press SELECT A NEW PHOTO to upload a picture, then press SAVE.',
                'Under Update Password, complete Current Password, New Password and Confirm Password and press SAVE.',
                'Under Two Factor Authentication, press Enable, confirm your password, scan the QR code with your authenticator app and store the recovery codes.',
                'Under Browser Sessions, press Log Out Other Browser Sessions if you have signed in on a shared computer.',
            ],
            'images' => ['profile' => 'The Profile page: Profile Information with photo, name and email, followed by Update Password'],
            'routes' => ['profile.show'],
        ],

        'The screen layout' => [
            'body' => '<p>Every page after sign-in shares the same frame: a dark green sidebar on the left, a white header across the top and the page content in the middle. Learning the frame once means every module feels familiar. This article names each part; the following article covers the controls inside the pages.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li><b>Sidebar brand header</b>: the corporation logo (from Settings) and the words <b>IFRS 9 ECL &amp; EIR Platform</b> in gold. Pressing the logo goes to the Dashboard.</li><li><b>Sidebar menu</b>: <b>Dashboard</b> and <b>Workspace</b> sit alone at the top. Below them the module groups are written in small capitals with a square icon tile and a chevron on the right. Press a group name to open or close it; a group that contains the page you are on opens by itself. Inside a group, sub-groups (for example <b>PD MODEL SETUP</b>) open the same way, and pages are indented with a small dot. The page you are on is highlighted with a gold bar on its left edge and a gold icon or dot.</li><li><b>Search</b>: the magnifier box at the left of the header. In this release it is a placeholder and does not search across the platform; use the <b>Search…</b> box on each list page instead.</li><li><b>Notification bell</b>: grey when there is nothing new; amber, ringing, with a red count badge when you have unread notifications. See the Notifications article.</li><li><b>Avatar menu</b>: your photo or initial in a circle. It opens a menu with <b>Profile</b> and <b>Log Out</b>.</li><li><b>Page heading</b>: the page title at the top of the content area, often with buttons on the right (a green period pill, <b>Download PDF</b>, <b>New Ticket</b> and so on).</li><li><b>Flash messages</b>: after an action, a green bar with a tick and the message (for example <b>Ticket #012 created successfully.</b>) or a red bar with a cross. When a form is rejected the red bar reads <b>There is one form error.</b> or <b>There are N form errors.</b> and lists the reasons. Press the small X at the right to dismiss.</li><li><b>Loading pill</b>: when a page takes more than a moment to load, a gold pill with a spinner and the word <b>LOADING</b> appears at the top centre; when the page arrives it turns green and reads <b>DONE</b> for half a second. Pages that load instantly show nothing.</li><li><b>Help button</b>: on pages that have page help, a round green question mark floats at the bottom right. See Getting help.</li></ul><h4>The error dialogue</h4><p>If an action cannot be completed the platform never shows a raw error page. Instead a white dialogue with a red warning icon explains what happened, shows an <b>Error code</b> line where one applies, and offers a green <b>OK, got it</b> button. The titles and messages are:</p><ul><li><b>No access rights</b>: You do not have the rights to view this page or perform this action. Contact your administrator if you believe you should have access. (code 403)</li><li><b>Session expired</b>: Your session has expired. Refresh the page and sign in again, then retry. (code 419)</li><li><b>Not found</b>: The item you tried to open no longer exists. Refresh and try again. (code 404)</li><li><b>Action could not be completed</b>: The file or request is too large to process. (code 413); Too many requests in a short time. Wait a moment and try again. (code 429); The system is temporarily unavailable. Please try again shortly. (code 503); The server hit an error while processing this action. It has been logged. (codes 500 and above); otherwise The server could not complete this action. Nothing was changed.</li><li><b>Connection problem</b>: Could not reach the server. Check your connection and try again. Nothing was saved.</li></ul><h4>On a phone or narrow window</h4><p>The sidebar is hidden. A three-line menu button (<b>Open sidebar</b>) appears at the left of the header; pressing it slides the same menu in from the left over a grey backdrop, with a white X (<b>Close sidebar</b>) at its top right. Tapping the backdrop also closes it. Tables scroll sideways inside their panel rather than the whole page.</p><h4>To sign out</h4><ol><li>Press the avatar at the top right.</li><li>Choose <b>Log Out</b>. You return to the sign-in page.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Nothing in the frame changes data by itself; only the page content does. The header search, bell and avatar are identical on every page.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The page is stuck on LOADING.</b> The server has not answered. Wait, then refresh the browser; if the <b>Connection problem</b> dialogue appears, check your network.</li><li><b>Session expired keeps appearing.</b> You were signed out (for example after a long idle period). Refresh the page and sign in again.</li><li><b>The sidebar shows a page I cannot open.</b> The menu is the same for every role; the <b>No access rights</b> dialogue means your role lacks that permission.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Find the page you need in the sidebar: press a group name in small capitals to open it, then press the page.',
                'Watch the gold LOADING pill at the top centre; the page has arrived when it turns green and reads DONE.',
                'Read any green or red flash bar under the page title, then press its X to dismiss it.',
                'If a dialogue with a red warning icon appears, read the title and message, press OK, got it, and follow the advice given.',
                'Press the bell for notifications and the avatar for Profile or Log Out.',
            ],
            'images' => ['workspace' => 'The shared frame: sidebar with the current page highlighted in gold, header with Search, bell and avatar, page title with a green period pill'],
        ],

        'Common controls and icons' => [
            'body' => '<p>The platform uses one design system, so a button, badge or icon means the same thing on every page. This article is the key to that system. Colours carry meaning: green is positive or complete, gold is a warning or something pending, red is adverse or destructive, grey is neutral or inactive. No other colours are used for status.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li><b>Panels</b>: white cards with a soft border hold every table and form.</li><li><b>Tables</b>: a dark green header band with white capitals for column names; alternate rows shaded light grey; the row under the pointer turns pale green. Number columns are right-aligned. A totals row is bold with a gold line above it. When there is nothing to show a single grey line reads, for example, <b>No portfolios found.</b></li><li><b>Filter bar</b>: a white card above a table with small capital labels and input or drop-down boxes. On the Dashboard and Workspace the filter is instead a green pill: a calendar icon marks a <b>Reporting Period</b> selector, a stacked-layers icon marks a <b>Portfolio</b> selector.</li><li><b>Search and filter</b>: many lists have a <b>Filter</b> button with a small triangle (opens a panel of drop-downs), a <b>Search…</b> box that searches as you type, and a <b>Reset</b> link that clears both.</li><li><b>Row action icons</b> at the right end of each row, each a small rounded square: green eye (<b>View</b>), gold pencil (<b>Edit</b>), red bin (<b>Delete</b>), grey icon (a neutral action such as reopen or download). Hover to read the exact title.</li><li><b>Badges</b>: rounded pills. Light green means active, done or favourable; solid green means fully complete or resolved; gold means pending, on watch or high priority; red means adverse, critical or an issue; grey means inactive, closed, system-set or stable.</li><li><b>KPI tiles</b>: white cards with a coloured left edge, a small capital label, a large value and, where relevant, a small exact amount beneath and a change chip. Hovering shows the full figure.</li><li><b>Chart / Table toggle</b>: a two-button switch (<b>Chart</b>, <b>Table</b>) on chart panels; the green half is the active view. Table view shows the same numbers as a list you can copy.</li><li><b>Export</b> buttons open a dialogue with options such as <b>Export Format</b> or <b>Export Mode</b>; the button reads <b>Exporting...</b> until the file is ready.</li><li><b>Confirmation dialogue</b>: any delete shows a dialogue with a red triangle icon, the question, a grey <b>Nevermind</b> button and a red button repeating the action name. Nothing is deleted until you press the red button.</li><li><b>Drafts and locks</b>: some records carry a lifecycle. Manual articles can be <b>Draft</b> (hidden from readers) or published. An approved EIR is <b>Locked</b>; a locked row shows <b>Locked</b> with the date and can only be reopened by an administrator through <b>Reopen locked EIR</b>. Locked figures feed the ECL discounting and cannot be edited in place.</li><li><b>Pagination</b>: <b>Previous</b>, page numbers and <b>Next</b> under long tables; the current page is highlighted, greyed links are unavailable.</li><li><b>Required fields</b> carry a red asterisk after the label.</li><li><b>Section titles</b> inside forms are small green capitals with a gold underline.</li></ul><h4>How numbers are written</h4><ul><li>Money is shown in the organisation currency set in Settings, with thousands separators and two decimals: <code>384,449,701.57</code>.</li><li>Negative amounts are shown in parentheses, accounting style: <code>(384,449,701.57)</code>, never with a minus sign.</li><li>Large KPI values are compacted to keep tiles readable: <code>384.45M</code>, <code>66.40B</code>, <code>950.0K</code>; the exact amount is printed underneath.</li><li>Percentages carry two decimals: <code>1.00%</code>. Changes between periods are given as a percentage for money and as points (<code>pts</code>) for ratios.</li><li>Periods are written year then month: <code>2025-11</code>.</li></ul><h4>To filter a list</h4><ol><li>Press <b>Filter</b> and choose values in the drop-downs, or type in <b>Search…</b>.</li><li>The table refreshes by itself a moment after you stop typing.</li><li>Press <b>Reset</b> to clear every filter.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Filters change only what is displayed; they never change data. Row actions, exports and confirmations act on one record and are written to the Audit Trail under Administration.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The eye, pencil or bin is missing on a row.</b> Your role lacks the matching view, edit or delete permission, or the record is locked.</li><li><b>Numbers look wrong by a factor of a thousand.</b> Read the small exact figure under a compacted KPI value, or switch the panel to <b>Table</b>.</li><li><b>A total is in parentheses.</b> It is negative. On a period without exposure the Net Carrying Amount can be negative.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Read a badge by its colour: green is good or done, gold is pending or on watch, red is adverse or an issue, grey is neutral or inactive.',
                'Use the row icons: green eye to view, gold pencil to edit, red bin to delete (a confirmation dialogue always follows).',
                'Filter a list with the Filter button and the Search… box; press Reset to clear.',
                'Switch a chart to Table when you need the exact figures.',
                'Read amounts as two-decimal accounting numbers; parentheses mean negative and M or B on a tile means millions or billions.',
            ],
            'images' => ['tickets' => 'A standard list: count tiles, Filter, Search… and Reset, badges in green, gold and grey, and the green eye, gold pencil and red bin row icons'],
        ],

        'Getting help' => [
            'body' => '<p>Help is built into the platform in three layers: a help button on individual pages, four full documents under <b>System Documentation</b> in the sidebar, and Support Tickets for anything the documents do not answer. This article explains each.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li><b>Page help button</b>: a round green button with a white question mark fixed at the bottom right of pages that have page help (the Dashboard, Loan Book, Imports, Clients, Portfolios, the PD and LGD screens, ECL Calculation, Users and Settings, among others). Its tooltip reads <b>Help</b>. Pressing it opens a white dialogue with the page\'s help title, the help text, and an X at the top right to close. If nothing has been written for that page the dialogue says <b>No help manual found for this page.</b></li><li><b>System Documentation</b> group in the sidebar with four pages: <b>User Manual</b>, <b>Administrator Manual</b>, <b>Technical Manual</b> and <b>Installation Guide</b>.</li><li>Each document page has the document title and subtitle at the top, a <b>Download PDF</b> button, a left-hand contents rail with a <b>Search this manual...</b> (or <b>Search this document...</b>) box and the chapter and article names, and the document itself on the right, starting with a cover page.</li><li>The cover shows the corporation logo, the document name, a document control block (<b>Version</b>, <b>Prepared</b>, <b>Owner</b>, <b>Approved by</b>, <b>Classification</b>) and the developer credit.</li><li>In the two manuals, every article shows its title, an <b>Updated</b> date, the text, numbered steps in green circles and figures with captions (<b>Figure 1.</b> and so on). Press a figure to enlarge it; press anywhere to close.</li><li>Users with the settings permission also see <b>Edit manual</b>, which opens the authoring screen for that manual.</li><li>The Technical Manual and Installation Guide show a grey <b>Revised</b> date badge instead of <b>Edit manual</b>, because they are maintained with the software rather than on screen. The Technical Manual ends with a live data dictionary read from the database.</li></ul><h4>Which document to read</h4><ul><li><b>User Manual</b>: day-to-day use for analysts and reviewers. This document.</li><li><b>Administrator Manual</b>: users and access, settings, financial and reporting periods, import governance, locks and support.</li><li><b>Technical Manual</b>: architecture, data model, calculation engines, security and operations, for ICT staff and auditors.</li><li><b>Installation Guide</b>: installing and configuring the platform in the MAIIC environment.</li></ul><h4>To find an answer in a manual</h4><ol><li>Open the sidebar, expand <b>SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION</b> and choose <b>User Manual</b>.</li><li>Type a word in <b>Search this manual...</b>; the contents rail and the articles shrink to those that mention it.</li><li>Press an article name in the rail to jump to it.</li><li>Press <b>Download PDF</b> to save the whole manual as a branded PDF with the same content.</li></ol><h4>To raise an issue or request a change</h4><ol><li>Open the sidebar, expand <b>ADMINISTRATION</b> and choose <b>Support Tickets</b>.</li><li>Press <b>New Ticket</b>, describe the problem or request, and press <b>Create Ticket</b>. The ticket gets a reference such as <b>#012</b> and both MAIIC and the developer follow it there. See the Support tickets article for the full procedure.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>Reading help changes nothing. The manuals are content in the database, so when an administrator edits an article the change is visible on screen and in the next PDF at once. The screenshots are refreshed from the live system whenever the interface changes.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>No help manual found for this page.</b> No page help has been mapped to that screen yet. Use the User Manual search instead, or ask an administrator to add a page mapping.</li><li><b>The manual has no published content yet. Use "Edit manual" to add chapters and articles.</b> The manual tables are empty on this installation; an administrator should run the manual seed or write the articles.</li><li><b>Download PDF is slow.</b> The PDF is built from the whole manual with every figure; allow a short wait.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'On a page with a round green question mark at the bottom right, press it to read the help for that page; press the X to close.',
                'For the full reference, open the sidebar, expand SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION and choose User Manual.',
                'Type a word in Search this manual... to narrow the contents, then press an article in the left rail.',
                'Press Download PDF to keep an offline copy.',
                'If the documents do not answer your question, expand ADMINISTRATION, choose Support Tickets and press New Ticket.',
            ],
            'images' => [
                'help' => 'The User Manual: contents rail with search, Edit manual and Download PDF buttons, and the cover page with document control',
                'help-admin' => 'The Administrator Manual uses the same reader',
                'docs-technical' => 'The Technical Manual shows a Revised date badge and a numbered chapter list',
                'docs-installation' => 'The Installation Guide',
            ],
            'routes' => ['help.index', 'help.admin', 'docs.technical', 'docs.installation'],
        ],
    ],
];
